[lis@chaos.cs.brandeis.edu (Elisabeth Riba) writes:]
[]I just ate some deep fried newt (Mmm, mmm good...) and my hands got so
[]slippery I can no longer wield any weapons or wear any rings.  How can
[]I wipe the grease off my hands?  Also, I'm new here...

it will wear off naturally (10 moves should do it). you should remember
this incident, it could help you later if you happen to try on a ring
that might stick to your ring-finger.

priestesses have the ability to recognize the blessed/cursed state of
items by inspection. that is a real advantage since you normally need
to find an altar (or lots of identify scrolls/spells) to do that.

wizards (my favorite, also) have that cloak of magic protection
(aka the trap-buster except for magic traps? ...) and the athame of
endless Elbereth engraving.

read the guidebook (if possible), talk to the oracle (start looking
around level 5), play all the character types (you'll notice slight
advantages that each has), consider explore-mode for awhile (nethack -x),
use common sense (i.e. a sword is a better weapon than a dagger, dress
like those hard to hit dwarves, etc ...), read rec.games.hack, and
try to think of ways to discover magic without hosing yourself (i.e.
reading a scroll of fire could cause your potions and scrolls to
disintegrate, reading a scroll of destroy armor will do just that, if
possible), and finally, only believe half of what Lucas posts here
... ummm, forget the last suggestion.

some final advice: the hackers here are more than willing to offer
advice (or spoilers) for _specific_ game situations ...

